  "caption": "Quinn's hip scan said \"labral tear\", the internet was not calming, and Quinn started planning a farewell party for squats.\n\nKay's take: labral tears show up on scans of many pain-free hips, so the scan doesn't always explain the pain. Many people improve with a long, progressive rehab program first.\n\nWhat can help: building hip and trunk strength (glutes and deep hip muscles), trimming deep bending and twisting rather than stopping, retraining squats and lunges gradually, skipping stretches that pinch the front of the hip, and giving rehab around three months.\n\nGet it checked if pain keeps going despite steady rehab, or the hip locks or gives way.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
